    "comments": [
      {
        "by": "gia",
        "date": "2025-02-03",
        "text": "We then spent the next few hours walking and exploring the city – I did about 30k steps!\n\nA lot of places in Budapest are free to visit such as Buda Castle and Fisherman’s Bastion. Cross over the bridge and take a stroll around Margaret Island. \n\nWe booked river cruise for the evening that included unlimited drinks. Fairly affordable, I think it was £20 and lasted about 2 hours and you can see the views of the city. The nightlife is pretty good in Budapest if you like to party. Not for me but we did visit a few places but I don’t really remember them so I can’t comment on that. I did get into an \"argument\" with someone over who felt more old but sadly I didn't meet any crackheads. I did get asked if I wanted some cocaine though!! (I obviously said no)  \n\nThe next day we did more exploring, mainly St Stephens Basilica (you have to pay for this, I think its about £7 but you can get it cheaper if you have your student card). We also went on the Ferris wheel where I forgot I have a fear of heights 😭 \n\nOne thing you must do without fail is walk outside the Parliament building at night. Free unless  you are paying to visit inside, but the outside is visually stunning. \n\nI’d definitely go back to visit the thermal baths and the chair lift.",
        "reactions": []
      }
    ]
