    "blurb": "It's new York, the big apple, the Yada Yada. Everybody's heard about it, everybody loves it. Kinda. Here's my week in the city that does indeed sleep.",
    "getThere": "It's new York, the big apple, the Yada Yada. Everybody's heard about it, everybody loves it. Kinda. Here's my week in the city that does indeed sleep. \n\nIt was freezing cold, so I spent a lot of my days inside working and eating porridge. And even though there's a million things to do, let me just highlight some of my favorites from the times I actually ventured outside. \n\nCentral park, you've heard of it. It's that central park. The home of ducks and geeze. Not as big as Chapultepec but a decent park nonetheless. I enjoyed the view surrounding the park. \nAfter a stroll was the stroll down Manhattan where I got to gander at all the \"famous\" marks. Some of which I gotta say I'm not sure why is that famous. But got to see empire state building, that central square with all the ads everybody loves for some reason with people in batman costumes plus a bunch of others. All them cheeky things. \nMy favourite landmark tho from this area was the famous Hilton, see photo. \n\nLater I got to walk through highline park before finishing the day as the sun was coming down in little island parks. Both of which I really loved. Top tier shit. \n\nNo trip to New York is complete of course without strolling down wallstreet and rubbing em balls for good luck before wandering on. One thing I wish I've seen on this trip that I couldn't as it was fenced off for some reason was the 9/11 memorials. Outside that tho, lots of fun views. Before walking across the Brooklyn bridge. Couldn't find the wanderlust sticker that was once slapped on it unfortunately. But got to walk a little around Brooklyn. \n\nOutside that, got a small taste of the nightlife. Never seen more funkier dancers and flashy dressers. It was a sight to be seen while tripping and vaping. 10/10 would do it again. \n\nCheers muchachos",
