        "text": "Robert Frost Trail- The trail is about 50 miles and is meant to celebrate the poet Robert Frost who lived in the area. It is a mix of more suburban and actual nature so not great for backpackers. \n\nHadley- The 2010 World Monuments Watch, marked the historic town as in danger, due to having no preservation measures. The town has a few spots for nice walks and a state park.\n\nQuabbin Reservoir- The main source of water for Boston, it is still accessible in many spots for certain but not all recreational activities. Many towns were flooded in the construction of the reservoir. Fall foliage is spectacular in the area. It is not located in Amherst but in the greater metro area.\n\nNorthampton- A great area for shopping and exploring. A small quaint New England Town",
