    "blurb": "Goa was a big touristy hub back in the day, and still is though most people prefer SEA now. It is connected by a sea pier and two airports as well as rail and road. The more adventurous can walk for pilgrimages :3",
    "getThere": "Goa was a big touristy hub back in the day, and still is though most people prefer SEA now. It is connected by a sea pier and two airports as well as rail and road. The more adventurous can walk for pilgrimages :3\n\nThings to see/do:\n\nI was here for different reasons again, but managed to get a trip out of it afterwards for a few days, with a lot of scootering around the town, amidst the harsh monsoon 😆\n\nI was in a nicer town of Goa called Anjuna with clean beaches and clean nightlife. When not hobbling around at midnight to random bars with live music, I was able to relax and get work done at the hostel. As always there was a lot of amazing food and drinks (even local!) involved and it was a great break from the monotony back home.\n\nI would definitely recommend South Goa for a first-timer though, as I’ve been there on another trip and it has a lot more tourists (non-local too) and prettier beaches!",
